{"fields":{"advisory":{"aliases":[],"categories":["crypto-failure"],"collection":"crates","cvss":null,"date":"2026-10-23","description":"## Summary\n\nThe `ctutils::Choice` type has mask generation functions for each unsigned\ninteger size (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`). These are `const fn` and\ntherefore can't reuse the `asm!`-backed mask generation in the `cmov` crate\nthat's otherwise used to ensure constant-time.\n\nIn releases prior to v0.4.4, the generated code from these functions could\ninclude a branch on commonly used platforms. This has been corrected in this\nrelease and now verified on several platforms using BINSEC.\n\nAdditionally, `u128` comparison operations provided via `ctutils::Choice` and\nintended to work in constant-time were generating branches on 32-bit targets.\nThis has been resolved via a special case implementation of these functions\nfor such targets.\n\n## Impact\n\nBranch instructions on secret values can potentially leak such values via\ncovert channels. This can enable attackers to potentially recover such secrets.\n\n## Resolution\n\nThis has been resolved by calling `Choice::to_u8()` when generating the mask,\nwhich in turn uses `black_box` as an optimization barrier. Verification that\nthis resulted in the desired change in the generated assembly across a variety\nof target CPU architectures was performed by BINSEC, which now runs\nautomatically in CI using `cargo checkct`.","expect-deleted":false,"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0385","informational":null,"keywords":[],"license":"CC-BY-4.0","package":"ctutils","references":[],"related":["RUSTSEC-2026-0003"],"source":null,"title":"Non-constant-time mask generation and `u128` comparisons","url":"https://github.com/RustCrypto/utils/pull/1569","withdrawn":null},"code":"vulnerability","graphs":[{"Krate":{"name":"ctutils","version":"0.4.3"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"crypto-bigint","version":"0.7.5"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"elliptic-curve","version":"0.14.1"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"ecdsa","version":"0.17.0"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"k256","version":"0.14.0"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"nsealr-core","version":"0.0.0"}}]}]},{"Krate":{"name":"k256","version":"0.14.0"},"repeat":true},{"Krate":{"name":"primeorder","version":"0.14.0"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"k256","version":"0.14.0"},"repeat":true}]}]},{"Krate":{"name":"primefield","version":"0.14.0"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"primeorder","version":"0.14.0"},"repeat":true},{"Krate":{"name":"wnaf","version":"0.14.1"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"k256","version":"0.14.0"},"repeat":true},{"Krate":{"name":"primeorder","version":"0.14.0"},"repeat":true}]}]}]},{"Krate":{"name":"sec1","version":"0.8.1"},"parents":[{"Krate":{"name":"elliptic-curve","version":"0.14.1"},"repeat":true}]}]}],"labels":[{"column":1,"line":11,"message":"security vulnerability detected","span":"ctutils 0.4.3 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"message":"Non-constant-time mask generation and `u128` comparisons","notes":["ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0385","Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0385","## Summary\n\nThe `ctutils::Choice` type has mask generation functions for each unsigned\ninteger size (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`). These are `const fn` and\ntherefore can't reuse the `asm!`-backed mask generation in the `cmov` crate\nthat's otherwise used to ensure constant-time.\n\nIn releases prior to v0.4.4, the generated code from these functions could\ninclude a branch on commonly used platforms. This has been corrected in this\nrelease and now verified on several platforms using BINSEC.\n\nAdditionally, `u128` comparison operations provided via `ctutils::Choice` and\nintended to work in constant-time were generating branches on 32-bit targets.\nThis has been resolved via a special case implementation of these functions\nfor such targets.\n\n## Impact\n\nBranch instructions on secret values can potentially leak such values via\ncovert channels. This can enable attackers to potentially recover such secrets.\n\n## Resolution\n\nThis has been resolved by calling `Choice::to_u8()` when generating the mask,\nwhich in turn uses `black_box` as an optimization barrier. Verification that\nthis resulted in the desired change in the generated assembly across a variety\nof target CPU architectures was performed by BINSEC, which now runs\nautomatically in CI using `cargo checkct`.","Announcement: https://github.com/RustCrypto/utils/pull/1569","Solution: Upgrade to >=0.4.4 (try `cargo update -p ctutils`)"],"severity":"error"},"type":"diagnostic"}
